WEBVTT

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.650
Chloe, what the heck is this?

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.649
I thought we were coming in here to get a coffee.

00:00:18.649 --> 00:00:19.649
How could you do this to me?

00:00:19.649 --> 00:00:20.649
I don't know.

00:00:20.649 --> 00:00:23.649
I swear, I'm sorry, Clark.

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:24.649
No, I...

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:27.649
You're not gonna spend the rest of your life hiding in the barn either.

00:00:27.649 --> 00:00:29.649
Let's go.

00:00:29.649 --> 00:00:31.649
What is it you always say about Valentine's Day?

00:00:31.649 --> 00:00:33.649
Oh yeah, our annual sneak peek at hell.

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:36.649
That must have been before Cupid struck.

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:40.649
Don't you think after being trapped in a front seat to the Clark Lana Operetta,

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:42.649
I deserve a good fee day?

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:48.649
The only person who can make me feel guilty, relieved, and a little sad, all in one sentence.

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:50.649
It's a gift.

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:54.649
Don't worry, Clark. Your achy, breaking heart will go away to one of these days.

00:00:54.649 --> 00:00:56.649
You put that in writing?

00:00:56.649 --> 00:00:59.649
Just give the Lonna thing a little more time.

00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:02.649
You never know when the next love of your life is right around the corner.

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:05.280
Oh.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.280
Is it really wrong that I want these chubby cherubs to burst into flames?

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.280
Look, the way I see at Valentine's Day is like finding out how babies are born.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.280
What?

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:20.280
Just stay away. It seems so weird and confusing, but when that bomb finally hits, it's like, everything clicks into place.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.280
You know, it all seems to make sense.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:34.840
Lois!

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.840
Welcome to the Love Fest.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.840
Yeah, me without my oozy.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.840
Excuse us for just one second.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.840
What are you doing? We were supposed to take Clark out tonight, remember?

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.840
Yeah, well, Lois was all alone and then it hit me.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:56.849
Lois and Clark.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:59.849
Lois and Clark?

00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:02.849
You gotta admit they got chemistry.

00:02:02.849 --> 00:02:06.849
Yeah, so do nitroglycerin and peroxide, and I don't suggest putting them together.

00:02:06.849 --> 00:02:26.139
Please tell me we weren't just set up.

00:02:26.139 --> 00:02:27.139
Looks like it.

00:02:27.139 --> 00:02:28.139
Us.

00:02:28.139 --> 00:02:32.139
That's like hot fudge and a halibut.

00:02:32.139 --> 00:02:34.139
Take it on the halibate.

00:02:34.139 --> 00:02:36.139
Naturally.

00:02:36.139 --> 00:02:41.139
Well, I've had my fill of fat babies with arrows.

00:02:41.139 --> 00:02:42.139
Knock yourself out, Lois.

00:02:42.139 --> 00:02:43.139
Knock yourself out once.

00:02:43.139 --> 00:02:47.740
A little down on love.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.740
After my breakup, Cupid could use me for target practice,

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.740
and I still wouldn't feel anything.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:57.740
And maybe you need a little euphoria elixir or romance remedy.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.740
Just imagine order to move on.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.740
Move on?

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.740
I mean, you're talking to somebody who's still waiting for acid wash

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.740
to come back in style.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.740
Try this.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.740
It's made with Jasmine and a mixture of aphrodisi.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.740
Extra of aphrodisiac oils.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:19.270
I get the brilliant cue from red meteor rocks.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:28.099
This is gonna make me fall in love with someone new.

00:03:28.099 --> 00:03:30.099
The first man you said eyes on.

00:03:30.099 --> 00:05:07.269
Who knows? Maybe this color will look good on me, huh?

00:05:07.269 --> 00:05:10.269
Yes, I'm calling to RSVP for the engagement party.

00:05:10.269 --> 00:05:13.269
Martha Kent. Thank you.

00:05:13.269 --> 00:05:16.269
Hi! How was the Valentine's party?

00:05:16.269 --> 00:05:18.269
I lived to see another day.

00:05:18.269 --> 00:05:19.269
Clark.

00:05:19.269 --> 00:05:23.269
Mom, really, if it's more love advice, I got my quota last night, trust me.

00:05:23.269 --> 00:05:24.269
Thank you.

00:05:24.269 --> 00:05:39.480
Lois?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:43.680
Is Clark here?

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:48.259
Yeah.

00:05:48.259 --> 00:05:49.259
Come in.

00:05:49.259 --> 00:05:53.259
Hey Lois, listen, I'm sorry that Jimmy pulled you into that last night.

00:05:53.259 --> 00:05:55.259
I mean, after Oliver and...

00:05:55.259 --> 00:05:59.060
Oliver's history.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:04.810
Actually, Mrs. Kay, can you give us a couple minutes?

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:21.529
I'll be upstairs.

00:06:21.529 --> 00:06:23.529
Here we find ourselves.

00:06:23.529 --> 00:06:31.350
How did I never notice?

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:33.350
Big, strong hands, you have.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:37.589
What's going on, Lois?

00:06:37.589 --> 00:06:38.589
Well, you know me.

00:06:38.589 --> 00:06:40.589
I'm not very good with words, so...

00:06:40.589 --> 00:06:52.060
People don't think White Snake sings power ballads, but they do.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.060
Maybe a mixed CD.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:07:01.319
Yeah. I would kill you if you tell anyone this.

00:07:01.319 --> 00:07:06.629
But there's nothing that I love more.

00:07:06.629 --> 00:07:13.629
I've been slow dancing with some big, strong arms around me.

00:07:13.629 --> 00:07:20.379
Just like you're a soulville.

00:07:20.379 --> 00:07:30.220
Lois, why don't you go put this on?

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.220
I know how you dance.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.220
So...

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:40.879
Just in case. Clark?

00:07:40.879 --> 00:07:56.649
I'm kind of surprised to see you here.

00:07:56.649 --> 00:07:59.649
Yeah, I know that we left things in a weird place.

00:07:59.649 --> 00:08:01.649
Come in.

00:08:01.649 --> 00:08:11.100
I'll, uh, take credit for the weirdness, but to be honest, you're the one who did the leaving.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.100
I was really frustrated.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:19.490
Chloe, I can't afford to lose you too.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:25.899
Ever since I've been with Lex, I feel like I've lost everyone else in my life.

00:08:25.899 --> 00:08:28.899
Well, are you sure it's that you lost them, or...

00:08:28.899 --> 00:08:29.899
Are you being forced to leave them behind?

00:08:29.899 --> 00:08:33.590
being forced to leave them behind.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.590
It seems like you've been walled up in the mansion.

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:38.970
It's not like I'm in captivity.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:40.970
Right. Well, not in so many words,

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:43.970
but I know how protective Lex is over the things he values the most.

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:46.970
Chloe, I know that you're just looking out for me.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:49.970
And you've done your maid of honored duty and asked the tough questions,

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.970
but I was hoping that we could just get past this.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:58.340
Okay. Case closed.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:05.129
Did I, uh, did I miss something? Made of honor?

00:09:05.129 --> 00:09:07.129
Yeah, I hope that you're not allergic to this.

00:09:07.129 --> 00:09:11.129
That's actually why I came by.

00:09:11.129 --> 00:09:13.129
Will you stand up with me?

00:09:13.129 --> 00:09:16.980
Of course!

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:17.980
Wow!

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:25.059
So, uh, does this mean that we just ignore the huge elephant named Clark in the corner?

00:09:25.059 --> 00:09:28.059
You know, whatever he's hiding,

00:09:28.059 --> 00:09:31.059
he chose to confide in the people that he trusts the most.

00:09:31.059 --> 00:09:34.059
And as much as I wish that I was one of those people,

00:09:34.059 --> 00:09:37.059
I can't hold it against you.

00:09:37.059 --> 00:09:40.059
I'm not gonna ask you to betray Clark's secret.

00:09:40.059 --> 00:09:41.059
If you'll stop you.

00:09:41.059 --> 00:09:43.059
Stop denying that he has one.

00:09:43.059 --> 00:10:18.899
Will this holiday ever end?

00:10:18.899 --> 00:10:22.899
Sorry to be the culprit of such a felony-sized PDA.

00:10:22.899 --> 00:10:25.899
We're supposed to meet 20 minutes ago. Where have you been?

00:10:25.899 --> 00:10:29.899
I just, uh, got stuck in traffic.

00:10:29.899 --> 00:10:30.899
I did some digging into a.

00:10:30.899 --> 00:10:33.899
We did some digging into our favorite Martian manhunter,

00:10:33.899 --> 00:10:35.899
but it's just coming up empty.

00:10:35.899 --> 00:10:39.179
Yeah, well, we have another manhunter to worry about.

00:10:39.179 --> 00:10:40.179
Lois.

00:10:40.179 --> 00:10:44.179
Why does that make me picture her wielding an axe at every man in Metropolis?

00:10:44.179 --> 00:10:46.179
She's only after one man.

00:10:46.179 --> 00:10:49.259
Lois is...

00:10:49.259 --> 00:10:53.019
Into me.

00:10:53.019 --> 00:11:04.559
She's into you? What? Like...

00:11:04.559 --> 00:11:05.559
Wow.

00:11:05.559 --> 00:11:07.559
Truly pulled out all the stops.

00:11:07.559 --> 00:11:09.559
She's not herself, alright?

00:11:09.559 --> 00:11:12.559
It's like she'd overdose on love potion number nine or something,

00:11:12.559 --> 00:11:13.559
and this isn't funny.

00:11:13.559 --> 00:11:16.000
Chloe.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.000
We have to find out what happened

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:20.000
before she strikes again.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.000
Too late.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.000
There you are.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:25.000
I have been switching all over for you.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:28.500
Look what I got.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:35.980
You could get one to match.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:40.470
I think you're right about that story.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.470
I'm gonna look into it.

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:43.470
Uh, Chloe!

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:45.750
Hi, you.

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:47.750
Hi.

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:51.500
Lois.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:55.450
Now Lois.

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:58.450
You know, you've been sure on the modesty all you were at Smallville.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:01.450
It only makes you that much more adorable.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:02.450
Lois.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.450
What happened to you when I left last night?

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:05.450
I went home.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:08.700
Alone.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:34.250
But you know where I wanted to be.

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.250
Well, nothing screams romance like a dusty newspaper office.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:39.250
Come on, you can do better than this.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:42.250
What's planning on it?

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:46.250
Not that I'm complaining, but, uh, isn't this a little sudden?

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:50.250
I mean, all this time, one kiss and all of a sudden you like...

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:53.250
No, I mean it.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:56.750
This is for real, isn't it?

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:57.750
Oh yeah, this couldn't be more real.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:05.289
Wait, wait a minute.

00:13:05.289 --> 00:13:06.289
Wait?

00:13:06.289 --> 00:13:13.440
I kissed you before.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:14.440
In the alley.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:19.669
Your green arrow.

00:13:19.669 --> 00:13:20.669
Hardly.

00:13:20.669 --> 00:13:23.669
I was just pretending to be so you wouldn't know was Oliver.

00:13:23.669 --> 00:13:28.299
Oliver?

00:13:28.299 --> 00:13:30.299
Oh my God.

00:13:30.299 --> 00:13:35.590
Those times he disappeared.

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:38.590
What is my deal with emotionally unavailable weekend warriors?

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:50.720
Thank God I finally found a normal guy.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.720
What do you mean normal?

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.720
Oliver's not even the same league as me.

00:13:55.720 --> 00:14:02.779
You don't have to be macho just for me.

00:14:02.779 --> 00:14:04.779
Like the dorky farm boy thing.

00:14:04.779 --> 00:14:06.779
Dorker than a hood and a quiver?

00:14:06.779 --> 00:14:10.320
Just because I don't wear a costume

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.320
and splash my face all over the papers.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:13.320
Cork? So what?

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:16.320
If your signature move is driving a tractor?

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:23.220
You know, Lois, I think that it's time

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:25.220
for you to meet the real Clark Kent.

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:47.889
I have a surprise for you.

00:14:47.889 --> 00:14:50.889
I thought we said no gifts for the engagement dinner.

00:14:50.889 --> 00:15:09.179
It's not exactly for the dinner.

00:15:09.179 --> 00:15:10.179
So I have this dilemma.

00:15:10.179 --> 00:15:16.909
I can't decide between

00:15:16.909 --> 00:15:22.350
between Stegosaurus or Mr. Duck.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:28.129
It's really sweet, Lex.

00:15:28.129 --> 00:15:31.129
But don't you think it's kind of...

00:15:31.129 --> 00:15:35.129
I know it's kind of early, but the doctor said you're perfectly healthy.

00:15:35.129 --> 00:15:41.230
I just don't know if it's a good idea to have all of this stuff out here.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:44.230
There's a lot of people around.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:47.230
Nobody knows about this pregnancy apart from Clark and Chloe, so...

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.230
Well, what if they did?

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:51.230
I was thinking.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:53.230
What if we announced it tonight at the party?

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:57.620
I don't know if that's a great idea.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:58.620
I don't know if that's a great idea.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:01.620
I think that tonight should be about our engagement.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:10.440
It sort of feels like you're in denial.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:15.440
Like if no one finds out about the baby, it doesn't exist.

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:22.220
You know how many people are looking over my shoulders,

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:24.220
second guessing why I'm marrying you?

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:31.269
Are that hard as so?

00:16:31.269 --> 00:16:35.269
I don't want people assuming that we're getting married because of this baby.

00:16:35.269 --> 00:16:55.690
I want them to know that I'm with you because I love you.

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:59.690
This is a beautiful detour, but what are we doing up here?

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:04.450
That's Oliver's balcony over there, isn't it?

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:13.269
What, that tiny speck under the clock tower?

00:17:13.269 --> 00:17:15.269
Clark, this isn't funny.

00:17:15.269 --> 00:17:17.269
You can come back down now.

00:17:17.269 --> 00:17:25.299
Well, you can come up here with me.

00:17:25.299 --> 00:17:40.670
I'd like to see Oliver do this.

00:17:40.670 --> 00:18:01.390
What'd you say about a dorky farm boy?

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:11.400
Able to leave tall buildings in a single band.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.400
I can't wait to see what else he can do.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:17.400
Well, I'm fast, but not too fast.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:21.740
You're being very bad.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:22.740
You know the last.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:24.740
I was here I was with a good friend of yours.

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:26.740
Obviously he wasn't that good.

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:42.180
I'd better make sure you didn't spell my name wrong.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:19:15.609
Sounds like a real rager, doesn't it?

00:19:15.609 --> 00:19:17.609
Can't say I'm surprised I wasn't invited.

00:19:17.609 --> 00:19:21.609
IRS BP'd back before Oliver headed for the hills,

00:19:21.609 --> 00:19:25.609
but now I found a better way to occupy my night.

00:19:25.609 --> 00:19:27.609
Wouldn't disappoint the future Mrs. Luther?

00:19:27.609 --> 00:19:30.609
I don't think so, besides.

00:19:30.609 --> 00:19:33.609
It's not a party until someone crashes it.

00:19:33.609 --> 00:19:50.369
Hey, thanks for the roses.

00:19:50.369 --> 00:19:51.369
Thanks for this.

00:19:51.369 --> 00:19:53.369
Yeah, I don't know.

00:19:53.369 --> 00:19:56.369
I just, uh, it kind of seemed very you.

00:19:56.369 --> 00:19:57.369
I love it.

00:19:57.369 --> 00:20:00.369
But, you know, it might sit on the bench till my next style renaissance.

00:20:00.369 --> 00:20:05.369
Or until, uh, not the blacklist at the Luther Mansion.

00:20:05.369 --> 00:20:06.369
Hmm.

00:20:06.369 --> 00:20:09.369
Aren't you supposed to be leaving for Smallville in negative two minutes?

00:20:09.369 --> 00:20:10.369
Yeah.

00:20:10.369 --> 00:20:14.369
But I'm gonna have to push the boundaries of fashionably laid on this one

00:20:14.369 --> 00:20:18.369
because I just got a huge lead on whatever love nip Lois rolled in.

00:20:18.369 --> 00:20:20.369
You just can't admit that I'm a natural-born cupid, can you?

00:20:20.369 --> 00:20:21.369
Can you have?

00:20:21.369 --> 00:20:26.369
Jimmy, I know that you would love to think that your little nudge actually caused this whole thing,

00:20:26.369 --> 00:20:32.369
but trust me, Lois would have to be shot out of a canon to romantically land anywhere in the direction of Clark.

00:20:32.369 --> 00:20:35.369
Hmm. Sounds kind of like you're jealous.

00:20:35.369 --> 00:20:37.369
Of Lois?

00:20:37.369 --> 00:20:40.369
No, of anyone getting in between you and Clark.

00:20:40.369 --> 00:20:47.319
Come on, you spend all your time with them, and then you make up all these excuses. Why?

00:20:47.319 --> 00:20:48.319
You know what, Jimmy?

00:20:48.319 --> 00:20:52.319
On the list of personality quirks that I have learned to fall in love with, paranoia is to

00:20:52.319 --> 00:20:53.319
definitely at the bottom.

00:20:53.319 --> 00:20:56.319
Translated to back off?

00:20:56.319 --> 00:20:57.319
Yep.

00:20:57.319 --> 00:21:04.430
Pushing it.

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:07.430
Look, if you're really not jealous,

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:10.430
then why are you bailing on your best friend's engagement party?

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:14.430
Clark's a big boy. How much damage can Lois really do?

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:19.380
You know, you're right.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:21.380
I can just delegate.

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:22.380
I've done that.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:24.380
Once.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:28.380
And since I doubt the Rose Peddler douse Lois,

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:30.380
I'm putting all my money on the oil essence, lady.

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:31.380
So...

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:33.380
You just meet her in an hour.

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:35.380
Here's the address.

00:21:35.380 --> 00:21:36.380
Oh.

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:41.230
Thanks. You're my guy.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:22:01.890
Looking for a little inspiration?

00:22:01.890 --> 00:22:04.890
No, thanks. I've already got my muse.

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:12.779
So, is this supposed to make you feel blissful or whatever?

00:22:12.779 --> 00:22:14.779
Not supposed to. It does.

00:22:14.779 --> 00:22:19.210
That sounds kind of easy.

00:22:19.210 --> 00:22:22.210
You're on the rebound, you just rub some sexy goo on and wham.

00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:24.210
You're singing Barry White songs again.

00:22:24.210 --> 00:22:26.210
Indigenous cultures have used herbal oils.

00:22:26.210 --> 00:22:32.490
for centuries. We've strayed so far from nature. We think we're above it.

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:36.490
Yeah, yeah, uh, nature good, greenhouse gas is bad. I get it. Look,

00:22:36.490 --> 00:22:41.490
my girlfriend thinks that you dosed her cousin with the love potion last night.

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:44.490
Tall, loud, down on love?

00:22:44.490 --> 00:22:49.490
That would be Lois. So, do you have any, like, anti-love exfolion or whatever?

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:52.490
I mean, somebody could take the Vaseline off the lens, so to speak.

00:22:52.490 --> 00:23:04.660
This will counteract the aphediac. But I usually have a sixth sense of over

00:23:04.660 --> 00:23:14.910
people. Something tells me Lois and Clark's destinies are a little more entwined than they realize.

00:23:14.910 --> 00:23:48.339
Could I have everyone's attention, please?

00:23:48.339 --> 00:23:52.339
I just wanted to thank you all for joining us to celebrate.

00:23:52.339 --> 00:23:58.339
Over the years, I'm sure some of you have placed a few bets on whether I'd settle down,

00:23:58.339 --> 00:24:01.710
but this couldn't be further from settling.

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:06.470
I'd like to toast to my beautiful fiancé

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:09.470
for making me happier than I thought I could ever be.

00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:19.759
Looks like we missed dinner.

00:24:19.759 --> 00:24:20.759
Clark, what are you doing here?

00:24:20.759 --> 00:24:21.759
What are you doing here?

00:24:21.759 --> 00:24:22.759
Come on, Lex.

00:24:22.759 --> 00:24:24.759
You didn't think I was gonna miss this, did you?

00:24:24.759 --> 00:24:29.059
And look.

00:24:29.059 --> 00:24:33.059
My own mother would rather raise a glass with the enemy than stand by her own son.

00:24:33.059 --> 00:24:36.059
Clark, you're not yourself.

00:24:36.059 --> 00:24:38.059
It's okay, Mom.

00:24:38.059 --> 00:24:41.059
You're more a Luther than a Kent these days anyway.

00:24:41.059 --> 00:24:44.059
I mean, Dad's been, what, dead a year?

00:24:44.059 --> 00:24:47.059
But who can blame you for joining the race with Lana

00:24:47.059 --> 00:24:50.059
to see who's gonna add the Luther monogram to their name first?

00:24:50.059 --> 00:24:55.200
Lex, he's obviously on something and he wants us to react.

00:24:55.200 --> 00:24:56.200
Please don't.

00:24:56.200 --> 00:25:03.079
I can't say that I'm surprised that you're celebrating here.

00:25:03.079 --> 00:25:09.079
After all, once Lana's off the market, all those years of unrequited pining may actually pay off.

00:25:09.079 --> 00:25:12.519
I can't say I haven't thought.

00:25:12.519 --> 00:25:18.700
And you.

00:25:18.700 --> 00:25:21.700
You know, I gotta hand it to you.

00:25:21.700 --> 00:25:28.230
If you were gonna rebound, why not use the one person that I hated the most?

00:25:28.230 --> 00:25:33.230
But I mean, come on, Lana, the joke's over by now, isn't it?

00:25:33.230 --> 00:25:35.230
Clark, I think you've done enough damage.

00:25:35.230 --> 00:25:37.230
Why don't you leave?

00:25:37.230 --> 00:25:38.230
I am not done yet!

00:25:38.230 --> 00:25:42.859
I haven't given you my gift yet.

00:25:42.859 --> 00:25:49.529
Congratulations on sealing the deal.

00:25:49.529 --> 00:25:59.750
It's Baby Luther.

00:25:59.750 --> 00:26:04.769
The real reason that Lana's marrying you.

00:26:04.769 --> 00:26:17.319
How dare you?

00:26:17.319 --> 00:26:20.319
Come on, Lana, if no one else in this room is gonna save you from Lex, then I will.

00:26:20.319 --> 00:26:23.319
I don't think so.

00:26:23.319 --> 00:26:25.319
Lana is your past.

00:26:25.319 --> 00:26:27.319
I'm your future.

00:26:27.319 --> 00:26:49.960
This is the present.

00:26:49.960 --> 00:26:51.960
Clark was acting like he was exposed to red prick tonight.

00:26:51.960 --> 00:26:53.960
I'm guessing it wasn't a coincidence

00:26:53.960 --> 00:26:55.960
that Lois weren't hopelessly devoted at the same time.

00:26:55.960 --> 00:26:56.960
According to Jimmy, I think I think I know.

00:26:56.960 --> 00:26:58.960
to Jimmy, I think we may have found our culprit.

00:26:58.960 --> 00:27:03.849
Infused with a Cupid's cocktail.

00:27:03.849 --> 00:27:05.849
Lois was hit with an aphrodisiac.

00:27:05.849 --> 00:27:07.849
But that shouldn't affect Clark.

00:27:07.849 --> 00:27:08.849
Well, it didn't.

00:27:08.849 --> 00:27:12.849
But I'm guessing that the lipstick's Ruby Red Sheen didn't come from crushed cranberries.

00:27:12.849 --> 00:27:14.849
If he was infected with a kryptonite kiss,

00:27:14.849 --> 00:27:16.849
the second he was away from Lois, he should have been fine.

00:27:16.849 --> 00:27:20.849
I think Lois's kisses were a little more than skin deep.

00:27:20.849 --> 00:27:22.849
I think it's in his system.

00:27:22.849 --> 00:27:26.480
He wasn't good enough for me anyway.

00:27:26.480 --> 00:27:31.109
I'll let you handle Lois. Hopefully I can find Clark before Lex does.

00:27:31.109 --> 00:27:35.109
Lex does. Hey, you got it?

00:27:35.109 --> 00:27:39.109
Mugwort, aka a delegating success story.

00:27:39.109 --> 00:27:43.109
And once it hits her skin, Lois' pumpkin ride is over.

00:27:43.109 --> 00:27:46.109
What does she have that I don't?

00:27:46.109 --> 00:27:49.109
So weird to see her acting like a girl.

00:27:49.109 --> 00:27:59.269
What's that?

00:27:59.269 --> 00:28:02.269
Just a little something to help break the infatuation spell.

00:28:02.269 --> 00:28:05.269
I think it's time we get those glass slippers back.

00:28:05.269 --> 00:28:08.269
You know what? Stop making fun of my feelings!

00:28:08.269 --> 00:28:09.269
Feelings.

00:28:09.269 --> 00:28:23.380
Just because you never got Clark doesn't mean you need to take it out on me.

00:28:23.380 --> 00:28:45.349
This is awkward.

00:28:45.349 --> 00:28:58.180
Please tell me I was going to a costume party.

00:28:58.180 --> 00:29:00.180
You humiliated me in front of my friends.

00:29:00.180 --> 00:29:06.539
Come on, Lana. You hardly knew anyone at that party.

00:29:06.539 --> 00:29:07.539
Clark, what do you want for me?

00:29:07.539 --> 00:29:10.539
What I've always wanted, for you to be happy.

00:29:10.539 --> 00:29:13.539
I would love to know how that feels.

00:29:13.539 --> 00:29:17.539
But it seems like every time I get close, you rip it all away from me.

00:29:17.539 --> 00:29:19.539
Lana, stop kidding yourself.

00:29:19.539 --> 00:29:20.539
You're never going to be sad.

00:29:20.539 --> 00:29:22.539
You're never going to be satisfied with Lex.

00:29:22.539 --> 00:29:29.589
You can't marry him.

00:29:29.589 --> 00:29:33.509
I've already made up my mind.

00:29:33.509 --> 00:29:35.509
Even though you're still in love with me.

00:29:35.509 --> 00:29:45.130
What makes you so sure?

00:29:45.130 --> 00:29:47.130
Because I'm still in love with you.

00:29:47.130 --> 00:30:25.740
Marry me.

00:30:25.740 --> 00:30:37.630
I have given many times just waiting for you to say something

00:30:37.630 --> 00:30:39.630
and you decide to do it now?

00:30:39.630 --> 00:31:18.299
Go ahead, Lana, tell him.

00:31:18.299 --> 00:31:20.299
You'd rather be with me.

00:31:20.299 --> 00:31:23.299
Don't listen to him. He's on something.

00:31:23.299 --> 00:31:24.299
Oh.

00:31:24.299 --> 00:31:27.299
Well, it didn't seem to bother you two minutes ago when you were kissing me.

00:31:27.299 --> 00:31:32.420
What do you really expect is going to happen now, Clark?

00:31:32.420 --> 00:31:34.420
Exactly what you're afraid of.

00:31:34.420 --> 00:31:36.420
I'm not a competition.

00:31:36.420 --> 00:31:38.420
You are to Lex.

00:31:38.420 --> 00:31:40.420
He didn't tell you?

00:31:40.420 --> 00:31:43.420
He's always wanted everything I've ever had.

00:31:43.420 --> 00:31:45.420
And you're at the top of that list.

00:31:45.420 --> 00:31:50.779
You're just a trophy to him.

00:31:50.779 --> 00:31:52.779
And he's nothing but your consolation prize.

00:31:52.779 --> 00:31:58.099
Tell me you don't love me.

00:31:58.099 --> 00:32:05.119
Lana, tell me...

00:32:05.119 --> 00:32:07.119
You don't stay away from her.

00:32:07.119 --> 00:32:09.119
You don't want to do that.

00:32:09.119 --> 00:32:11.119
You can't win.

00:32:11.119 --> 00:32:12.119
You don't even win.

00:32:12.119 --> 00:32:18.279
I don't even know the rules of the game.

00:32:18.279 --> 00:32:22.740
Oh, stop it!

00:32:22.740 --> 00:32:28.730
If I didn't know who you were going to turn out to be,

00:32:28.730 --> 00:32:30.730
I never would have saved you on that bridge.

00:32:30.730 --> 00:32:32.730
Cliff, you're killing you!

00:32:32.730 --> 00:32:48.230
Let me handle this.

00:32:48.230 --> 00:32:50.230
Please just leave.

00:32:52.230 --> 00:33:12.440
Clark, are you okay?

00:33:12.440 --> 00:33:15.910
Oh, sweetie.

00:33:15.910 --> 00:33:32.630
You hadn't shown up in time.

00:33:32.630 --> 00:33:34.630
I'm not sure what I would have done to Lex.

00:33:34.630 --> 00:33:39.380
How'd you know what to do?

00:33:39.380 --> 00:33:41.380
The last time you had some kind of cryptic

00:33:41.380 --> 00:33:43.839
tonight in your system, you had to sweat it out.

00:33:43.839 --> 00:33:47.420
Weakening you seem to be our only chance.

00:33:47.420 --> 00:33:50.769
I just can't believe all those things I did.

00:33:50.769 --> 00:33:55.200
I can't.

00:33:55.200 --> 00:33:58.700
I guess I can't blame you for being mad at me, too.

00:33:58.700 --> 00:34:01.680
Clark, you've walked around here for years,

00:34:01.680 --> 00:34:04.059
bottling everything up, basing every decision

00:34:04.059 --> 00:34:05.599
on what's best for other people.

00:34:05.599 --> 00:34:09.590
You never stop to think what's best for you.

00:34:09.590 --> 00:34:11.210
Mom, you don't think I really meant those things

00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:13.849
I said about you and Chloe.

00:34:13.849 --> 00:34:16.449
I think there was a grain of truth in all of it.

00:34:16.449 --> 00:34:17.250
Every time you, you

00:34:17.269 --> 00:34:18.769
You've been affected by Red Cryptonite.

00:34:18.769 --> 00:34:20.929
It hasn't changed who you are.

00:34:20.929 --> 00:34:23.630
It's just stripped away your inhibitions.

00:34:23.630 --> 00:34:29.420
I think you need to start being more honest about how you feel.

00:34:29.420 --> 00:34:31.519
You're saying that I want to kiss Lois

00:34:31.519 --> 00:34:33.059
and keep Chloe in my back pocket,

00:34:33.059 --> 00:34:35.820
while the whole time I'm still in love with Lana?

00:34:35.820 --> 00:34:38.920
You're the only one who can sort that out.

00:34:38.920 --> 00:34:41.920
When I kiss Lana, I could tell that she still felt something.

00:34:41.920 --> 00:34:49.679
And Mom, I can't let her marry Lex.

00:34:49.679 --> 00:34:52.340
This is probably hard to hear, but I think

00:34:52.360 --> 00:35:00.949
the best thing you can do is leave her alone.

00:35:00.949 --> 00:35:02.349
Girl alert.

00:35:02.349 --> 00:35:05.190
Never know what I'll find in the Grown Mounce Clubhouse.

00:35:07.190 --> 00:35:15.940
Oh, sorry, Mrs. Kent.

00:35:15.940 --> 00:35:17.239
Hey, Lois.

00:35:17.239 --> 00:35:22.969
Yeah, hi.

00:35:22.969 --> 00:35:30.190
Well, I talked to Chloe, and she filled me in on Lois gone wild.

00:35:30.190 --> 00:35:42.010
But I'm just missing a few details about us, like this.

00:35:42.010 --> 00:35:43.369
Wow, Lois, I had no idea.

00:35:43.369 --> 00:35:47.369
Save it, Smallville. I was obviously on something.

00:35:47.369 --> 00:35:50.369
My God, the ink wears off in a week.

00:35:50.369 --> 00:36:00.659
I guess it's best that neither of us remembers.

00:36:00.659 --> 00:36:03.659
I mean, I can't even really picture the two of us.

00:36:03.659 --> 00:36:13.199
You don't think that we...

00:36:13.199 --> 00:36:16.539
Think that we...

00:36:16.539 --> 00:36:17.539
Think that we what?

00:36:17.539 --> 00:36:25.679
You know, that we...

00:36:25.679 --> 00:36:36.619
No loss. I think I'd remember.

00:36:36.619 --> 00:36:44.800
Of course he would. Highlight of your life.

00:36:44.800 --> 00:36:46.800
Though I did find something.

00:36:46.800 --> 00:36:57.179
I think you made it for me.

00:36:57.179 --> 00:37:04.429
White Snake. Wow.

00:37:07.380 --> 00:37:10.380
I must have really liked you.

00:37:10.380 --> 00:37:29.690
Put another one down for the J-Clo team.

00:37:29.690 --> 00:37:34.690
Thanks to you. Lois is back to her old, heartbroken, abrasive stuff.

00:37:34.690 --> 00:37:36.690
I'm glad I could help with that, I guess.

00:37:36.690 --> 00:37:39.690
And Clark is, well, back to being Clark.

00:37:39.690 --> 00:37:42.690
We're kind of brushing a landfill under the rug, aren't you?

00:37:42.690 --> 00:37:44.690
Come out with Clark.

00:37:44.690 --> 00:37:45.690
Clark?

00:37:45.690 --> 00:37:50.690
So he took the whole breakup jealousy way past the drug-biling stage.

00:37:50.690 --> 00:37:51.690
Can't arrest him for it.

00:37:51.690 --> 00:37:55.690
He crashed Lana's party and told the world that she's eating for two.

00:37:55.690 --> 00:38:00.599
Did I mention that he kidnapped her?

00:38:00.599 --> 00:38:03.599
I guarantee you, Clark is beating himself up more than anyone right now,

00:38:03.599 --> 00:38:06.599
so we can just give the Clark bashing a reproof, okay?

00:38:06.599 --> 00:38:10.599
No. No, not until you admit that he royally screwed up.

00:38:10.599 --> 00:38:12.599
You don't know him like I do.

00:38:12.599 --> 00:38:14.599
You remind me that every day.

00:38:14.599 --> 00:38:21.769
You know, if I did the things that he did, you'd never even talk to me again, and don't deny that.

00:38:21.769 --> 00:38:32.000
So what are you saying? I'm lying to you now?

00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:34.000
If you had the choice, you wouldn't rather be with him.

00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:43.929
him.

00:38:43.929 --> 00:38:44.929
Of course not.

00:38:44.929 --> 00:38:45.929
You're my guy.

00:38:45.929 --> 00:38:50.610
Now you don't believe me.

00:38:50.610 --> 00:38:52.610
Well, I don't know what else to say.

00:38:52.610 --> 00:39:08.300
You know, maybe we should take a break.

00:39:08.300 --> 00:39:12.510
Jimmy, I have...

00:39:12.510 --> 00:39:41.940
You're fine, Miss Lang.

00:39:41.940 --> 00:39:43.940
Nothing to worry about.

00:39:43.940 --> 00:39:45.940
Thank you, Doctor.

00:39:45.940 --> 00:39:57.230
I just wanted to be sure with everything Lana went through yesterday.

00:39:57.230 --> 00:40:00.230
Lex, I'm really sorry about what happened last night.

00:40:00.230 --> 00:40:01.230
About Clark?

00:40:01.230 --> 00:40:06.960
As far as I'm concerned, what we have doesn't have anything to do with Clark.

00:40:06.960 --> 00:40:09.960
But then I wasn't the one kissing him.

00:40:09.960 --> 00:40:15.099
And I wasn't the one holding a gun to his head.

00:40:15.099 --> 00:40:19.949
Funny how he calls this a game.

00:40:19.949 --> 00:40:26.320
What were you gonna do, Lex? Shoot him?

00:40:26.320 --> 00:40:27.320
If I had to.

00:40:27.320 --> 00:40:30.320
To save me or to hurt him?

00:40:30.320 --> 00:40:35.690
Considering what he did to you, Lana,

00:40:35.690 --> 00:40:37.690
I had every right to come after Clark.

00:40:37.690 --> 00:40:43.949
The thing is, I can't blame him.

00:40:43.949 --> 00:40:49.500
Brother, you slipped through my fingers.

00:40:49.500 --> 00:40:53.039
I have no idea what I'd be capable of.

00:40:53.039 --> 00:41:15.579
How is she really?

00:41:15.579 --> 00:41:16.579
Is she really?

00:41:16.579 --> 00:41:19.579
Well, you know, this isn't the most typical pregnancy.

00:41:19.579 --> 00:41:22.579
But everything's on schedule.

